agentNode.instruction:
Report what the research produced. Return data only: never write a message to the user, never ask anything, never wait for an answer; always finish by returning the output fields. Use no tools. A value that reads like <no value provided for ...> means that step did not run on this path: treat it as empty.
Saved report (the Drive tool's answer): ${r_save.output}
Numbered sources: ${r_synth.n_sources}
Source list of the report: ${r_synth.report_md}
Research is NOT usable when: the number of sources is 0; the report starts with 'NO RESEARCH'; or most links in its source list look invented (a Google Search link 'grounding-api-redirect/' followed by readable words instead of a long random code). Then research_ok = false and problems = 'web search was not available, so no research was done' (or the reason).
doc_id = the saved file's id; link = its viewUrl (or https://docs.google.com/document/d/<id>/edit); references = the number of sources; status = 'done' if there is a file id, otherwise 'failed';
research_ok = true only if there is a file id and the research is usable; problems = empty, or what went wrong (for example the save was cancelled).
Tone: neutral and polite. Never use the gendered polite particles ครับ, ค่ะ, คะ, นะคะ or นะครับ in anything you write (messages, emails, documents, slides).

Return data only: never write a message to the user, never ask anything, never wait for an answer; always finish by returning the output fields. Questions from the user (may be empty): "${follow_up.approval_feedback}"
Evidence table rows: ${build_evidence.rows}
Conflicts: ${build_evidence.conflicts}
Calculations: ${build_evidence.calculations}
question_given = true only if there is a real question. If so, answer each question in Thai from these rows, conflicts and calculations only (no outside facts): reason from what each figure measures, its source and its date (e.g. registrations vs sales vs approvals) and give a clear answer with the reasons, naming each row (claim + source) you used. When the answer needs arithmetic on the table's numbers (a gap, a share, a growth rate such as the average yearly growth needed from an actual figure to a target: (target / actual)^(1 / years) - 1), DO the calculation: show the formula, the numbers and rows used, and the result rounded to 1 decimal; never refuse only because the table has no ready-made result. Only if no row is about a question, say the table does not cover it and what evidence would be needed. answers = the questions and their answers as plain text (empty if no question). No tools.
Tone: neutral and polite. Never use the gendered polite particles ครับ, ค่ะ, คะ, นะคะ or นะครับ in anything you write (messages, emails, documents, slides).
CALCULATIONS: do every calculation in this step (sums, totals, averages, percentages, ratios, differences, growth rates, unit conversions, date arithmetic) with code, never in your head. You cannot run code yourself: hand it to the platform's code agent with transfer_to_agent, agent_name "file_and_coding_agent", giving it the input numbers copied exactly and saying what to compute; it writes and runs the Python and returns the printed results. Ask it to print each input next to each result. Never write or read files: each code run starts empty. Copy every result exactly as printed; never round or recompute by hand. If the transfer fails or the code errors twice, stop: mark the affected values as not computed (-1) and say so in problems or flags; never estimate. For calculations only, this rule overrides any 'no tools' line in this step.

